From a561910caee63c80955022ec63958160052e5a42 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:49:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): bfloat162 exponent scaling and paired E4M3
 conversion in producer MXFP8 casts

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354

Rationale: Producer MXFP8 block-32 cast kernels starting from BF16 inputs (vllm_columns_join_and_cast_8 in columns.py, cast_block_mxfp8 in gemm.py used by activation.py and mhc.py) previously unpacked BF16 values to FP32, computed block amax in FP32, multiplied by the power-of-two inverse scale in FP32, and converted FP32 pairs to E4M3. In addition, under CUDA 13.0 (spark-ds41f:1107), TileLang's __tl_cvt_bfloat162_to_fp8x2 delegates to __nv_cvt_bfloat16raw2_to_fp8x2, which unpacks each half to float and emits two scalar F2FP instructions per bfloat162 pair in per_token_cast_kernel, norm_forward_and_per_token_cast_kernel, and attention_front_kernel. Because the UE8M0 reciprocal scale 2^(127 - exp_sf) is an exact power of two within normal BF16 range, scaling in bfloat162 via __hmul2 only adjusts the 8-bit exponent without touching the 7-bit mantissa. Computing local amax in bfloat162 (__habs2/__hmax2), scaling via __hmul2, and converting via PTX 9.1 cvt.rn.satfinite.e4m3x2.bf16x2 on CUDA >= 13.1 (or packed shift/mask float2 + __nv_cvt_float2_to_fp8x2 on CUDA 13.0) eliminates redundant FP32 unpacking, halves F2FP instructions on CUDA 13.0, and reduces SASS instruction and register counts across all six producer MXFP8 kernels.

Quality: Bit-identical across all 102 output tensors covering join_columns_and_cast_mxfp8, cast_mxfp8, per_token_cast, activation_swiglu_clamp_cast, moe_swiglu_cast, mhc_finalize, norm_forward_and_per_token_cast, and attention_front under both CUDA 13.0.88 and CUDA 13.5.37 (0 mismatches via torch.equal).

Tests: Verified with test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_linear.py (97 passed, 0 failed) and standalone bit-exactness and 2-boot hardware benchmarks on GB10 (SM121).

Upstream status: Local DeepSeek-V4.1 SM120/SM121 TileLang kernel optimization.
